19s2|n|The sixtieth part of an hour; sixty seconds. (Abbrev. m.; as, 4 h. 30 m.) ; The sixtieth part of a degree; sixty seconds (Marked thus ('); as, 10¡ 20'). ; A nautical or a geographic mile. ; A coin; a half farthing. ; A very small part of anything, or anything very small; a jot; a tittle. ; A point of time; a moment. ; The memorandum; a record; a note to preserve the memory of anything; as, to take minutes of a contract; to take minutes of a conversation or debate. ; A fixed part of a module. See Module. ; To set down a short sketch or note of; to jot down; to make a minute or a brief summary of.	n:1hhn,67,4~1hhn,67,4
