1a9f|v|To cause a promiscuous interpenetration of the parts of, as of two or more substances with each other, or of one substance with others; to unite or blend into one mass or compound, as by stirring together; to mingle; to blend; as, to mix flour and salt; to mix wines. ; To unite with in company; to join; to associate. ; To form by mingling; to produce by the stirring together of ingredients; to compound of different parts. ; To become united into a compound; to be blended promiscuously together. ; To associate; to mingle.	o:1o5r,69,3~1o5r,69,3
